# Intent: Train 2 item 6, the low-battery ladder (features.md Always-on). 20 percent on the battery: one chirp. 10 percent: a chirp, a short request on the face ("Battery low. Please charge me.", English or Spanish by the face language) and a `battery` event with step=ask that the host says aloud. 5 percent: a `battery` event with step=sleep, the words on the face, and the unit powers itself off 8 s later if it is still on the battery at 5 percent or less. Each step fires once per discharge, only after three one-second readings agree, never on a failed read (level 0), and a cable in re-arms every step and blocks them all. A unit that boots at 8 percent fires the request only. One test tool, self.battery.simulate, drives the ladder without draining the battery; its simulated 5 percent step never powers the unit off. Rides one 1 s tick on the existing stackchan task: no task, no timer, no heap.
# Placement: unit (battery is read on the robot; the host half is only the spoken line for the ask event)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan.cc of the StackChan main component (MIT); firmware/main/hal/hal.cpp (MIT)
# Check after a flash: self.battery.simulate level=19 gives one chirp and a battery event step=chirp; level=9 gives the ask with the words on the face; level=4 gives step=sleep and a log line saying the unit would power off; level=-1 returns to the gauge. On a cable no step fires.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_LOW_BATTERY (default y); off removes the ladder and the tool.
